-- so the third case disagrees too. Three molecules, three different reasons: valine's two methyls are
-- exchanged by the graph and separated by the configuration, leucine's two methyls and two beta
-- hydrogens both are, and isoleucine's methyls are separated by the graph itself while its methylene
-- hydrogens are not. The construction gives the right count in each case from the same two definitions,
-- and the field's single canonical identifier gives the first count in all three.
il-counts-differ : class-count Ile il-eq il-rank il-graph-gens 22 il-h ≡ class-count Ile il-eq il-rank il-conf-gens 22 il-h → Empty
il-counts-differ q = seven-not-eight (concat (sym il-signals-graph) (concat q il-signals-conf))
